    "done_when": "per §4's 2026-10-07 comment, read-only: before any ssh call create /tmp/sshwrap/ssh as a script that execs /usr/bin/ssh -F $HOME/.ssh/config with all arguments, chmod +x it, export PATH=/tmp/sshwrap:$PATH, and require ssh -o BatchMode=yes jt-60sa hostname to succeed; from the graph, group the JT-60SA Document nodes at scored or discovered by source prefix (host plus the first four path segments) with counts, and pick ten sample filenames spread across those prefixes; on jt-60sa (nakasvr26) list the candidate web roots with ls -d /var/www/* /srv/* /opt/* /data* and never enter user home directories; then, for each of the ten sample filenames and each directory that listing returned, run exactly one bounded search, timeout 60 find with -maxdepth 8 and -name set to that filename, and record every hit; check whether a TWiki or Foswiki installation exists on nakasvr26 and where its pub directory is; from nakasvr26 run curl -sI against two sample https URLs that point at the nakasvr23 web server to see whether a redirect or mirror answers; report for each source prefix whether a migrated location was found, the old-to-new path mapping when one exists, and how many waiting documents it would cover; scripts and output in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-codex/twiki-attachment-probe/; write the evidence fragment and commit it with a conventional subject and body; no graph write, no discover run, no code change, and no host command beyond the bounded ones named here",
